## Phase 13: CssValue Subclass Specialization
Introduce specialized `CssValue` subclasses to eliminate boxing, reduce allocations, and improve type safety for common value types. Follow the pattern established by `CssEnumValue<T>`.

### 13.1 CssListValue (COLLECTION) — High Priority
Lists are extremely common: `font-family`, `background`, `transition`, `transform`, `box-shadow`, etc.
- [ ] Create `CssListValue` subclass with direct `CssValue[]` storage
- [ ] Add `ReadOnlySpan<CssValue> Values` property for allocation-free iteration
- [ ] Add indexer `this[int index]` and `Count` property
- [ ] Override `AsCollection()` to return existing array wrapped (or direct span access)
- [ ] Override `TryFormat()` for space/comma-separated serialization
- [ ] Override `Serialize()`, `Equals()`, `GetHashCode()`, `HasValue`
- [ ] Support separator metadata (space vs comma-separated)
- [ ] Update `CssValue.From(params CssValue[])` to return `CssListValue`
- [ ] Add tests for CssListValue

### 13.2 CssStringValue (STRING) — Medium Priority
Strings are common in custom properties, `content`, quoted `font-family` names.
- [ ] Create `CssStringValue` subclass with direct `string` storage
- [ ] Override `AsString()` for direct access (no cast)
- [ ] Override `TryFormat()` with proper CSS string escaping/quoting
- [ ] Override `Serialize()`, `Equals()`, `GetHashCode()`, `HasValue`
- [ ] Update `CssValue.From_String()` to return `CssStringValue`
- [ ] Add tests for CssStringValue

### 13.3 CssUrlValue (URL) — Low Priority
- [ ] Create `CssUrlValue` subclass with direct `CssUrl` storage
- [ ] Override `AsUrl()` for direct access
- [ ] Override serialization methods
- [ ] Update `CssValue.From_Url()` to return `CssUrlValue`
- [ ] Add tests for CssUrlValue

### 13.4 CssCalcValue (CALC) — Low Priority
- [ ] Create `CssCalcValue` subclass with direct `CssCalcExpression` storage
- [ ] Override `AsCalcExpression()` for direct access
- [ ] Override serialization methods
- [ ] Update factory method to return `CssCalcValue`
- [ ] Add tests for CssCalcValue

### 13.5 CssFunctionValue (FUNCTION) — Low Priority
- [ ] Create `CssFunctionValue` subclass with direct `CssFunction` storage
- [ ] Override serialization methods for function syntax
- [ ] Update factory method to return `CssFunctionValue`
- [ ] Add tests for CssFunctionValue

### 13.6 Cleanup & Optimization
- [ ] Audit remaining `data.ObjectValue` usages for potential subclass candidates
- [ ] Consider sealing base `CssValue` class or making constructor internal-only
